      "rev_n_7_ab1caf_0": {
        "revision_id": "rev_n_7_ab1caf_0",
        "node_id": "n_7_ab1caf",
        "thought_text": "Analyze the operation as a modular arithmetic problem: the sequence of values is N % K, |N % K - K|, etc., which effectively cycles between N % K and K - (N % K). The minimum is simply min(N % K, K - (N % K)).",
        "parent_revision_path_hash": "4113237671331844313",
        "replaces_revision_id": null,
        "feedback_id": null,
        "created_at": 1794506455.5828378
      },
      "rev_n_8_d295c3_0": {
        "revision_id": "rev_n_8_d295c3_0",
        "node_id": "n_8_d295c3",
        "thought_text": "Use a mathematical shortcut: since the operation is equivalent to moving towards 0 or K, the answer is the distance from N to the nearest multiple of K, which can be calculated directly without iteration.",
        "parent_revision_path_hash": "4113237671331844313",
        "replaces_revision_id": null,
        "feedback_id": null,
        "created_at": 1794506455.5828536
      },
      "rev_n_9_2788c6_0": {
        "revision_id": "rev_n_9_2788c6_0",
        "node_id": "n_9_2788c6",
        "thought_text": "Simulate the process iteratively but optimize by stopping early once the value drops below K/2, as further operations will only increase the value or cycle back to the same small set of values.",
        "parent_revision_path_hash": "4113237671331844313",
        "replaces_revision_id": null,
        "feedback_id": null,
        "created_at": 1794506455.5828624
      },
      "rev_n_10_5cf978_0": {
