      "rev_n_23_d66118_0": {
        "revision_id": "rev_n_23_d66118_0",
        "node_id": "n_23_d66118",
        "thought_text": "Consider the case where N is already less than K. In this scenario, the first operation yields K - N, and the second yields |(K - N) - K| = N, creating an immediate cycle between N and K - N. The answer is min(N, K - N).",
        "parent_revision_path_hash": "-3564268311801868196",
